0,Mande languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mande_languages,"The Mande languages are a family of languages spoken in several countries in West Africa by the Mandé peoples. They include Maninka, Mandinka, Soninke, Bambara, Kpelle, Jula, Bozo, Mende, Susu, and Vai.","Maninka, Sankaran",Niger-Congo
